<title>USA: Cemex CFO Caballero dies in New York.</title>
<headline>Cemex CFO Caballero dies in New York.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico-based cement giant Cemex S.A. said Sunday that its Chief Financial Officer Gustavo Caballero died in New York early on Saturday.</p>
<p>In a brief statement, the Monterrey-based company said Caballero had been diagnosed in August with lung cancer.</p>
<p>&quot;Arrangements are being made in Monterrey,&quot; it said. Further details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>Cemex is the world's third-largest cement company, according to industry analysts. It has expanded aggressively in recent years from its base in Mexico and now has operations in countries such as the United States, Spain, Venezuela, Colombia and Panama.</p>
